# Reversible execution demo
# Run this with: eric reverse examples/reverse_demo.eric
#
# The program computes fib(10) = 89
# Then the reversible execution engine replays every step backward,
# recovering the original input.
#
# This is possible because the interpreter records a trace of every
# state-changing operation (push, pop, assign, print) and can
# apply the inverse of each operation in reverse order.

fib(0) = 1
fib(1) = 1
fib(x) = add(fib(sub(x, 2)), fib(sub(x, 1)))

fib(10)
print
